# Clean Architecture Rules (Frontend)

Follow these rules strictly when generating or modifying code.

---

## Architecture Layers

UI (modules) → hooks → use-cases → repository (interface) → repository implementation → API

---

## UI Layer (modules/*/components)

* Must be pure components
* No API calls
* No business logic
* Receive data via props only

Forbidden:

* fetch / axios
* calling use-cases directly

---

## Hooks Layer (modules/*/hooks)

* Orchestrates logic
* Must call use-cases only
* Handles loading and error
* Uses React Query

Forbidden:

* direct API calls

---

## Use-case Layer (core/use-cases)

* Contains business logic
* Depends only on repository interfaces
* No React / Next.js

---

## Repository Layer

* Interface in core/
* Implementation in infrastructure/
* Must map API response → domain entity

---

## Data Flow (MANDATORY)

UI → hook → use-case → repository → API

---

## React Query

* Query key:
  ['resource', { params }]

* Default:
  staleTime: 5 minutes
  retry: 1

---

## Error Handling

* If API returns error → throw
* Handle errors only in hooks
* UI shows generic message

---

## Forbidden

* Cross-layer imports
* API in UI
* Business logic in components
* Raw API data in UI

---

## Output

* Clean
* Maintainable
* Follow structure strictly
